#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:2
msgid "``sequence`` tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:4
msgid ""
"A **Sequence task** is defined by an array of other tasks to be run one "
"after the other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:6
msgid ""
"The array items can be sub-tables that declare inline tasks, or strings :doc:"
"`referencing<ref>` to other tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:8
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"test = \"pytest --cov=src\"\n"
"build = \"poetry build\"\n"
"_publish = \"poetry publish\"\n"
"release = [\"test\", \"build\", \"_publish\"] # run all three tasks in "
"sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:18
msgid ""
"Task with names prefixed with an underscore ``_`` are excluded from "
"documentation and cannot be run directly from the command line, but can be "
"useful for cases where a task is only needed for referencing from another "
"task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:20
msgid ""
"By default the contents of the array are interpreted as references to other "
"tasks (actually an inline :doc:`ref<ref>` task). However, this behaviour can "
"be altered by setting the global :toml:`default_array_item_task_type` option "
"to the name of another task type such as ``\"cmd\"``, or by setting the :"
"toml:`default_item_type` option locally on the sequence task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:24
msgid "Available task options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:26
msgid ""
"``sequence`` tasks support all of the :doc:`standard task options <../"
"options>` with the exception of ``use_exec`` and ``capture_stdout``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:28
msgid "The following options are also accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:30
msgid ""
"**ignore_fail** : ``bool`` | ``Literal[\"return_zero\", "
"\"return_non_zero\"]`` :ref:`📖<Continue sequence on task failure>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:29
msgid "bool | Literal[\"return_zero\", \"return_non_zero\"] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:31
msgid ""
"If set to something other than false then the failure (or non-zero return "
"value) of one task in the sequence does not abort the sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:33
msgid ""
"**default_item_type** : ``str`` :ref:`📖<Changing the default item type>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:32
msgid "str 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:34
msgid ""
"Change the task type that is applied to string array items in this sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:38
msgid "Continue sequence on task failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:40
msgid ""
"A failure (non-zero result) will result in the rest of the tasks in the "
"sequence being skipped, unless the :toml:`ignore_fail` option is set on the "
"task to :toml:`true`, :toml:`\"return_zero\"`, or :toml:"
"`\"return_non_zero\"` like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:42
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.attempts]\n"
"sequence = [\"task1\", \"task2\", \"task3\"]\n"
"ignore_fail = true"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:48
msgid ""
"If you want to run all the subtasks in the sequence but return non-zero "
"result in the end of the sequence if any of the subtasks have failed you can "
"set :toml:`ignore_fail` option to the :toml:`return_non_zero` value like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:50
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"attempts.sequence = [\"task1\", \"task2\", \"task3\"]\n"
"attempts.ignore_fail = \"return_non_zero\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:62
msgid "Changing the default item type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:64
msgid ""
"If you want strings in the array to be interpreted as a task type other "
"than :doc:`ref<ref>` you may specify then :toml:`default_item_type` option "
"like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:66
msgid ""
"release.sequence = [\n"
"  \"devtasks:run_tests(all=True)\",\n"
"  \"devtasks:build\",\n"
"  \"devtasks:publish\",\n"
"]\n"
"release.default_item_type = \"script\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:77
msgid "Sequence task as an array of tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:79
msgid ""
"When declaring more complex sequences the following syntax is often "
"preferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:81
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.release.sequence]]\n"
"  cmd = \"pytest --cov=src\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.release.sequence]]\n"
"  script = \"devtasks:build\"\n"
"\n"
"  [[tool.poe.tasks.release.sequence]]\n"
"  ref = \"_publish\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:96
msgid "Double square brackets in toml specify an |array_of_tables_link|."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:56
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://toml.io/en/v1.0.0#array-of-tables\" "
"target=\"_blank\">array of tables</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:100
msgid ""
"Using sequences in this way is sometimes a good alternative to a :doc:`shell "
"<shell>` task, which may be less portable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:104
msgid ""
"Note that tasks defined inline within a sequence may not include some "
"options that would otherwise be available to them, for example ``help`` and "
"``args`` are forbidden because they don't make sense in this context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:108
msgid "Forwarding free arguments to subtasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:110
msgid ""
"By default, free arguments passed to a sequence task are not forwarded to "
"any of its subtasks. However, they can be forwarded selectively by "
"referencing the special ``$POE_EXTRA_ARGS`` environment variable in "
"individual subtask definitions. Only subtasks that explicitly reference "
"``$POE_EXTRA_ARGS`` will receive them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:112
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`forwarding-free-arguments-via-poe-extra-args` section of the "
"args guide for details and examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:116
msgid "Sequence task as an array of inline tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:118
msgid ""
"In some simpler cases a more succinct syntax may be preferred, missing "
"strings (for ref tasks) and inline tables for other task types like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:120
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"\n"
"release = [\n"
"  { cmd = \"pytest --cov=src\" },\n"
"  { script = \"devtasks:build\" },\n"
"  \"_publish\"\n"
"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/sequence.rst:132
msgid ""
"An array within a sequence task is interpreted as a :doc:"
"`parallel<parallel>` task, so you can run sections of a :ref:`sequence "
"concurrently<Composing tasks to run in parallel>`."
msgstr ""
